import mundane theorem stdlib/numbers/nonneg-or-neg
import mundane theorem stdlib/reasoning/or-left
import mundane theorem stdlib/reasoning/or-right

theorem average-at-most-an-end
  metamath    avgle
  note        The average of two numbers is at most the larger one: if B is
              not below A it is at most B, and otherwise at most A.
  let A ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let B ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  then (A + B)/2 ≤ A or (A + B)/2 ≤ B

1.  B − A ≥ 0 or B − A < 0
    mun:nonneg-or-neg x := B − A

2.  (A + B)/2 ≤ A or (A + B)/2 ≤ B
    cases, from 1

    case
    assume B − A ≥ 0                                                  (C1)

    2.1.  (A + B)/2 ≤ B
          inequalities
            B − A ≥ 0          C1
            2·B ≥ A + B        adding A + B
            B ≥ (A + B)/2      multiplying by 1/2
            (A + B)/2 ≤ B      symmetry

    2.2.  (A + B)/2 ≤ A or (A + B)/2 ≤ B
          mun:or-right, from 2.1

    case
    assume B − A < 0                                                  (C2)

    2.3.  (A + B)/2 ≤ A
          inequalities
            B − A < 0          C2
            A + B < 2·A        adding 2·A
            (A + B)/2 < A      multiplying by 1/2
            (A + B)/2 ≤ A      weakening

    2.4.  (A + B)/2 ≤ A or (A + B)/2 ≤ B
          mun:or-left, from 2.3
